era &gt; preview it is pegged to max frequency. This leads to higher than &gt; expected power consumption(2W+). &gt;  &gt; The camera stack is probably doing some heavy handed sync operations &gt; which causes the GPU to be always stuck at max frequency. &gt; This is a temporary fix until the userspace(camera) is either &gt; fixed or optimized because we may incur a performance penalty due to &gt; this change. &gt;  &gt; This bug is discussed here[1]. &gt;  &gt; 1. https://bugs.freedesktop.org/show_bug.cgi?id=110750 &gt;  &gt; BUG=b:130638275 &gt; TEST=Build and boot on octopus build is successful. &gt;  &gt; Change-Id: I802a9b0a1f5883e20eabcef0b832a97c495fc014 &gt; Signed-off-by: Azhar Shaikh &lt;azhar.shaikh@intel.com&gt; &gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/third_party/kernel/+/1633381 &gt; Reviewed-by: Stphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; &gt; Commit-Queue: Stphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; &gt; Tested-by: Stphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt;  Bug: b:135553743 Change-Id: I52a6cea3c51585800d2d4b895ac2202e63782882 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/third_party/kernel/+/1660289 Reviewed-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Commit-Queue: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Auto-Submit: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 15a5087f78ec1beaba3d59a8d057d9698182f5e8) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1687172 Tested-by: Ren-Pei Zeng &lt;kamesan@chromium.org&gt; Commit-Ready: Ren-Pei Zeng &lt;kamesan@chromium.org&gt; Legacy-Commit-Queue: Commit Bot &lt;commit-bot@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="1687172" owner_email="kamesan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/72/1687172/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I35e83a78c81c5d29f2d32a2e2d0febaec03b3249" commit="98b1862e584d945b7d75bc84c9339e84bef51547" commit_message="nebraska: Allow AppData with partial or empty AppID  The current problem is when we generate the payload properties from the payload itself, we don't have access to the appid of the payload. So the appid value would be empty. However, we still need to match based on appid. But for now we can relax the requirement of the matching by allowing appid match partially. Partial means if the AppData had an empty or partial appid, we sub-string check it against the request appid and if it was a sub-string, we consider that a match. This would work for many of our current situations specially for the platform updates where there is only one payload so matching with an empty appid should work.  BUG=chromium:920404 TEST=unittest TEST=send a request with a valid APP ID to a nebraska that has AppData with empty APP ID and response was correct. Same for an AppData with a substring of the request's APP ID.  Change-Id: I35e83a78c81c5d29f2d32a2e2d0febaec03b3249 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1674247 Tested-by: Amin Hassani &lt;ahassani@chromium.org&gt; Commit-Ready: Amin Hassani &lt;ahassani@chromium.org&gt; Legacy-Commit-Queue: Commit Bot &lt;commit-bot@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Norvez &lt;norvez@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Amin Hassani &lt;ahassani@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="1674247" owner_email="ahassani@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/dev-util" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/dev-util" ref="refs/changes/47/1674247/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I24e169fa72140f2ef9beb21a2da515f14abf74aa" commit="0ee7219c65647e73eaa24def27b605d588dbdeed" commit_message="CRAS: cras-sys: have cargo run handle all codegen  Update cras-sys's gene